---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DraftNote from '../../components/DraftNote.astro';
import { NAME, CURRENT_POLICY_URL } from '../../brand';
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description={`${NAME}’s privacy policy. A placeholder until the site’s own policy is written.`}
  stickyCta={false}
>
  <article class="section">
    <div class="wrap-narrow stack legal">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="tag">Placeholder</p>
      <p class="lede">
        This page will hold {NAME}’s privacy policy. Until it does, the policy that applies is the one for the optional
        account service: <a href={CURRENT_POLICY_URL}>read the current privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        In plain words, while you wait: {NAME} runs on your PC, has no telemetry, and sends nothing anywhere unless you
        choose a feature that needs to. <a href="/privacy">Privacy and data</a> lists each of those features and what it
        sends.
      </p>

      <h2>What the full policy will cover</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Who is responsible for {NAME} and how to contact them</li>
        <li>The app: what it stores on your PC, and what the features you switch on send, and to whom</li>
        <li>The optional account: what it holds, why, for how long, and how to delete it</li>
        <li>This website: no cookies, no analytics, and the server logs the host keeps</li>
        <li>Your rights under UK and EU data protection law, and how to use them</li>
        <li>How changes to the policy are announced</li>
      </ul>

      <DraftNote>
        Waits on the name and the legal operator (plan §10.2): the policy names who runs {NAME}, and moves here from the
        account service, whose URLs keep answering for installed builds. Terms of use go beside it at /legal/terms.
      </DraftNote>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal h2 {
    margin-top: 24px;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
  }
  .legal ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 6px;
    color: var(--t-fg-80);
  }
  .legal .tag {
    justify-self: start;
  }
</style>
